#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Beyond the Holy City runs the Smorodina, the river of fire between the living world and Nav, and every horde that comes is fed from across it. The Kalinov Bridge is the old way over it: built whole and sealed with the Ritual Arch, it lets the volkhvs close the crossing for good. The hordes know this, and will throw everything at the city on the night the arch is bound."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Foundation Stones"
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Bring back a relic of the old builders from an ancient site: their mark, set in the first stone, lets the foundation lie on the burning bank."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The Smorodina can't be bridged on common stone. The old builders left their first stones among the ruins they abandoned, and only stones that remember the old rites will rest on the fire's bank."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The Oak Piers"
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Clear a monster lair: the volkhvs won't raise an axe in the grove while the beasts are there."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The piers are cut from the sacred oaks of the grove, but beasts of the North have made their lairs among the roots and nobody can fell a tree while they howl."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The Iron Span"
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The forge is lit from the Holy City's own flame: weather a wave without the city losing Sanctity, or the flame gutters and the iron cracks."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The ore comes through the passes: hold a pass or a fort on a horde's road, so the smiths know the road can be kept."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Iron forged under Svarog's eye carries the road over the fire. The forge must burn without break, fed by ore brought in through the passes."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The Guardian Rails"
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The guardians' faces are copied from the old idols: bring back their likeness from an ancient site."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "A rail is quenched in the blood of a beast of the North: clear a lair to give the carvers what they need."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The rails are carved with the faces of guardians so that nothing from Nav can climb onto the bridge, and every rail must be quenched before it will hold."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The Ritual Arch"
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Forge the ritual torc from a Svarog's Ember: the volkhvs bind the arch with it, and without it the bridge is only a road for the enemy."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The arch at the far end closes the crossing. It is bound with a torc of Svarog's fire, and once it stands, everything beyond the river will come at once: Ritual Night."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Bring back a relic"
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Explore an ancient site while this stage is open."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Clear a monster lair"
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "An army clears a lair of the North while this stage is open."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Weather a wave unscathed"
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "A wave ends without the Holy City losing Sanctity since this stage began."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Hold a strong point"
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Win a field battle at a choke point or from a fort while this stage is open."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Craft the ritual torc"
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "Forge the ritual torc from a Svarog's Ember."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "With the arch sealed, the volkhvs begin the rite that will close the crossing for good. Every horde in Nav feels it. Tonight they all come at once, from every front, to break the city before the last words are spoken."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The Kalinov Bridge holds"
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The last horde broke against the walls and the rite was finished. The bridge over the Smorodina is sealed, Nav is shut, and the bells of the Holy City ring for the first time in a generation. The old faith lives on, because you held."
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The Holy City has fallen"
msgstr ""

#: data/bridge.json
msgid "The walls are breached and the sanctuary fires are out. The hordes pour across the Smorodina unopposed. Some of the people escaped into the forests, carrying the songs with them; perhaps one day they will try again."
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Elder's Hall"
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "The heart of the village. Each level opens another building slot and builds a little faster; every few levels add a place in the build queue and another outpost."
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Woodcutter"
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Cuts wood in the forest around the village."
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Quarry"
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Breaks stone from the hills around the village."
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Farm"
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Grows grain, which feeds the village and its troops."
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Iron Mine"
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Digs iron for weapons, armour and walls."
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Storehouse"
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "How much of each resource the village can keep; what comes in above it is lost."
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Barracks"
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Trains soldiers. Each level trains them faster, and higher levels open stronger troops."
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Scout Lodge"
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Trains scouts, who ride out to see a horde before it arrives."
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Caravan Yard"
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Keeps caravans to carry resources to allies and to the Holy City vault; each level adds more."
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Settlers' Lodge"
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Trains settlers, who walk out to found new villages."
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Studies the techs of the research tree; what you learn helps all your villages."
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "A camp on a nearby hex that gathers what the land gives: wood in forests, stone and iron in hills and mountains, grain on plains and lakes."
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Granary-Temple"
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "The stag-folk's own: a temple granary that brings in grain and feeds the troops for less."
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Stone Redoubt"
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "The bear-folk's own: a stone keep that makes the garrison harder to break."
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Longhouse Hall"
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "The wolf-folk's own: a longhouse where warriors eat less and train faster."
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Walls"
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "The walls round the village: hordes must break or climb them before they reach the garrison. Higher levels change wood for stone."
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Archer Tower"
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "A tower on the walls: its archers make the garrison strike harder while the walls stand."
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Gate Tower"
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Strengthens the gate, so the walls take longer to batter down."
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Ballista Platform"
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "A great crossbow on the walls that smashes the horde's siege engines."
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Murder Holes"
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Openings over the gate to rain stones on the attackers: the garrison defends better while the walls stand."
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Moat"
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "A moat before the walls: it keeps off battering and climbers and slows the building of siege engines; at higher levels it holds water."
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Watchtower"
msgstr ""

#: data/buildings.json
msgid "Sees hordes coming from farther away, so the warning comes sooner."
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Rod Jelena"
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Stag"
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "The stag-folk of the river meadows: first to sow, first to harvest, their villages grow like spring grass. They were never riders."
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Its arms are those of Nizhny Novgorod (1781): a red stag walking, on silver."
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Grain and fast village growth"
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Weak cavalry"
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Rod Rysa"
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Lynx"
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "The lynx-folk of the deep woods strike from the shadows of the trees and are gone before the horde can turn. Their elders trust old ways over new learning."
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Its arms are those of Gomel (granted in 1781): a gold lynx lying, on blue."
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Wood and ambushes"
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Slower research"
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Rod Medvěda"
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Bear"
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "The bear-folk of the iron hills dig deep and build thick walls. They are slow to leave the den they have made."
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Its arms are those of Yaroslavl (1672): a black bear upright with a gold poleaxe, on silver."
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Iron and fortifications"
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Slower expansion"
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Rod Bobra"
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Beaver"
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "The beaver-folk know every river and ford; their barges carry what the roads cannot. Their homes are built for trade, not for siege."
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Its arms are those of Bobrov (1781): a beaver in its own colour, on silver."
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Caravan speed and capacity"
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Weaker fortifications"
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Rod Sokola"
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Falcon"
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "The falcon-folk of the open steppe ride fast and see far; their scouts come home when others do not. They have little patience for stonework."
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Its arms are those of Sokołów Podlaski (seal of 1764): a falcon on an oak branch with a gold ring in its beak, on gold."
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Cavalry and scouts (fewer scout losses)"
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Costlier forts"
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Rod Volka"
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Wolf"
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "The wolf-folk of the northern stone fields know the cold and the things that come out of it. Their thin soil feeds them poorly."
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Its arms are those of Vovchansk (1781): a silver wolf running over green ground, on blue."
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Stone and cold resistance (against the North)"
msgstr ""

#: data/clans.json
msgid "Weaker grain"
msgstr ""

#: data/difficulty.json
msgid "Story"
msgstr ""

#: data/difficulty.json
